# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_lineshift_symbol_mapping.py" "LINE-SHIFT SYMBOL-MAPPING GATE: PASS" "line-shift symbol mapping (silent-miss fix)" "line-shift symbol mapping (audit r3 launch-blocker fix): the finer-collision engine now parses the BASE-side (-a,b) of each diff hunk header, NOT the new-side (+c,d). On origin/main a PR that added/removed net lines ABOVE an edit shifted the edit's NEW-side line numbers off its base symbol -> the edit mapped onto the WRONG base-version symbol span -> a REAL same-symbol collision silently dropped to 'clear' (and two PRs' new-side numbers lived in different coordinate frames, so the conflict-overlap test was meaningless too). The freshness key could NOT catch it (the PR base genuinely equals the analyzed graph; the shift is WITHIN the PR). BASE-side ranges align with main's base-version symbol spans + are comparable across PRs (all relative to the same main); pure-insertion hunks (-a,0) touch no base lines -> file-level fallback (recall-safe); content-free (line numbers only). This gate drives the REAL parser + the REAL gate path (act_for_claim -> main_impact_surface): a contained line-adding hunk no longer shifts a later same-symbol edit, and two PRs editing foo's base line are CAUGHT (serialize), not a silent 'clear' -- RED on origin/main (both 'clear'), GREEN after the fix" "line-shift symbol-mapping silent-miss closed: base-side hunk ranges so a contained line-adding hunk can't shift a later edit onto the wrong base symbol; the same-symbol collision serializes instead of a false 'clear'; recall-safe + content-free" 24
